\section{Proposed prospective tests}\label{sec:tests}
This initial audit motivates the proposed tests in Table~\ref{tab:tests}, for an evaluation window of 1 December 2026--30 April 2027. This is not an executable preregistration: current scripts contain fixed historical windows, and T1 lacks alert-to-batch identifiers. Before evaluation, authors must approve the protocol, specify missing-data denominators and averaging semantics, implement issue-time joins and the past-six-hour T2 rule, and freeze versioned code. Thresholds informed by this audit are exploratory; changes and failed tests must be published. We make no promise that the present scripts can be rerun unchanged.

\begin{table*}[t]
\caption{\textbf{Proposed tests for the 2026--27 evaluation window; implementation and author approval pending.} Baselines are this paper's results. Proposed ``pass'' criteria are stated here; ``if not'' is what the system does about a failure. CI is a 95\% interval; CAMS is the bias-corrected forecast.}\label{tab:tests}
\centering\sffamily\footnotesize
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{3.8pt}\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.1}
\begin{tabular}{@{}l p{4.0cm} p{3.9cm} p{4.3cm} p{4.0cm}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{} & \textbf{Question} & \textbf{Baseline (this paper)} & \textbf{Pass} & \textbf{If not}\\
\midrule
T1 & Is each eligible severe alert accepted by Telegram within 35 minutes? & Not established; next-broadcast timing does not verify membership or acceptance & At least 95\%, linking alert IDs to batch IDs and successful recipient responses; include failed/unmatched alerts & Diagnose queue and send failures before changing batching\\
T2 & Do persistent alerts predict a subsequent daily exposure window? & Not established; prior same-day outcome rates had invalid missing-data denominators & Define a forward 24-hour target and completeness rule; compare all alerts with a past-six-hour persistence rule; proposed lower CI limit 50\% & Retain a watch tier; do not present hourly snapshots as a daily exposure forecast\\
T3 & Does the corrected forecast beat carrying the last observation forward two days ahead? & MAE difference {{a4.leads.2.mae_diff_cor_minus_persistence.mean|sf2}} (CI {{a4.leads.2.mae_diff_cor_minus_persistence.ci[0] .. a4.leads.2.mae_diff_cor_minus_persistence.ci[1]|sf2}}), worse than carrying forward & Upper CI limit of the difference below zero & Stop issuing the second-day warning; show it as a range, not a value\\
T4 & Does upwind fire predict next-day \pmtf{} in the upper north, February--April? & $\rho={{a8.next_day_pm25_vs_upwind_upper_north.rho|f2}}$ (CI over days {{a8.next_day_pm25_vs_upwind_upper_north.ci[0] .. a8.next_day_pm25_vs_upwind_upper_north.ci[1]|f2}}; {{a8.next_day_pm25_vs_upwind_upper_north.days|int}} days), {{a8.next_day_pm25_vs_upwind_upper_north.rho_province_centred_only|f2}} without day-centring & $\rho\ge0.25$ with the lower CI limit above zero, over at least 60 days & Describe the indicator as a map of sources only, and drop it from the verdict\\
T5 & Do cameras track \pmtf{} within a camera over time? & Median within-camera $\rho={{a5.within_camera_rho.median|f2}}$ & Median $\rho\ge0.30$ among cameras with at least 20 judged frames & Remove the rule that lets cameras raise a province to WATCH\\
T6 & Does low visibility at airports separate smoky from clean hours? & {{a6.p_reduced_by_band[3].share|pct0}} of hours under 10~km at 25--37.5 against {{a6.p_reduced_by_band[0].share|pct0}} below 10; one airport supplies {{a6.p_reduced_by_band_cluster[3].largest_airport_hour_share|pct0}} & Gap of at least 20 points, cluster CI above zero, no airport over 30\% of hours & Keep visibility as a reason on the card and never in the score\\
T7 & Does success mean data? & Two token-gated sources logged 100\% success and wrote no rows & Zero token-gated sources that skip silently & A skipped source is reported as ``not configured'' on the status page\\
